      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T22:13:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried increasing it significantly, to 0x1000000 since txt starts 0x1008000 on my test image. It worked fine until after kernel booted and then faulted on address 0xffff here: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/cros_system/cros_system_npcx.c;l\u003d406. NPCX_REVISION_ADDR\u003d0xfffc, which is a magic address I guess? Since it must be a power of 2, 0x8000 is the largest allowed value that doesn\u0027t cause the fault. \n\nI think 0x400 is a good default pending Nuvoton input.",
      "parentUuid": "852b980d_c604bd1d",
